   $q$Which statement best expresses the author's central idea?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Students who type with ten fingers write faster than students who use two.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Computers have changed the way students learn and work in every school subject.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-broad"},{"text":"Middle schools should teach typing because it helps students in school and later in life.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Students learn to type well on their own by using computers and phones at home.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-counterclaim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Middle schools should teach typing because it helps students in school and later in life.$q$, $q$The author states the claim in paragraph 1 and supports it with reasons about speed, writing quality and jobs. The choice saying students learn to type well on their own is the opposing view the author argues against in paragraph 4.$q$, 'draft', '8510d3c9-cba2-54cb-a6a7-c020dd42b14d')
