   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The author argues that middle schools should teach typing because it makes students faster, improves their writing and prepares them for jobs. The author also claims self-taught habits are hard to fix.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Typing classes make students write faster and earn better grades in every subject. Students who take these classes also get better jobs as nurses and engineers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-unsupported-detail"},{"text":"Many students type with two fingers. Some people believe students learn to type at home, and many jobs today require people to write on a keyboard.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-central-claim"},{"text":"The author makes a convincing case, and any student who still types with two fingers is wasting time. Schools that skip typing classes are letting their students down.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The author argues that middle schools should teach typing because it makes students faster, improves their writing and prepares them for jobs. The author also claims self-taught habits are hard to fix.$q$, $q$The choice beginning "The author argues that middle schools should teach typing" states the author's claim and main reasons and labels them as the author's views. The choice beginning "Many students type with two fingers" lists details but never says what the author is arguing.$q$, 'draft', '8510d3c9-cba2-54cb-a6a7-c020dd42b14d')
