   $q$Why did the father sparrow ask Brightwing for help?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He was too tired to fly back to the elm.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-subject"},{"text":"Her branch had cracked and fallen onto his nest.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-sequence"},{"text":"A storm had torn his family's nest apart.","is_correct":true},{"text":"His chicks wanted to see her shiny treasures.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A storm had torn his family's nest apart.$q$, $q$The second paragraph says "a storm tore their nest apart," so he asked for shelter. Brightwing's branch cracks later, in the summer, and it is Brightwing who is too tired to fly.$q$, 'draft', '307deb04-66a0-5e03-8377-4cd6637e31ea')
