values
  ('77fbf059-4d6c-5416-9511-32fa2885bc28', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g6-theme-summary'), null, 'easy',
   $q$Which choice is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Mateo gives the most interesting presentation in his class, and his teacher should give him an award.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"For a history project, Mateo learns about old trolley lines, finds traces of them in town and shares a map showing how they still shape the streets.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Mateo and Mrs. Abernathy dig up the old trolley tracks and put them on display at the museum.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-false-detail"},{"text":"Mateo finds a rusty rail near the post office and kneels down beside it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$For a history project, Mateo learns about old trolley lines, finds traces of them in town and shares a map showing how they still shape the streets.$q$, $q$An objective summary covers the main events from beginning to end without judging them. The rail near the post office is only one detail, and the opinion about an award does not belong in a summary.$q$, 'draft', '14fcc73f-3c0a-5788-a24e-329e490e74c3')
