values
  ('5b0f7df4-0bdb-5c92-b0f6-cba42b8e914c', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g6-theme-summary'), null, 'easy',
   $q$Which choice is the best objective summary of the fable?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A lazy cricket and snail refuse to help, and they should be ashamed of themselves.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"When the moon stays hidden, a firefly uses her small light to guide a lost beetle, and other fireflies join her to light his way home.","is_correct":true},{"text":"A beetle gets lost, and the moon comes out to light his path back to his log.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"A firefly named Pip thinks her glow is no brighter than a grain of sugar.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$When the moon stays hidden, a firefly uses her small light to guide a lost beetle, and other fireflies join her to light his way home.$q$, $q$The correct summary tells the problem, Pip's action and the result without judging anyone. The moon only appears after everyone is asleep, so it does not light the beetle's path.$q$, 'draft', '825b3092-fb82-5c21-bd93-b8164252b46a')
