   $q$How does Lucia's way of practicing change over the story, and how does this develop the theme?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She goes from practicing every night to skipping practice, showing she has lost interest.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-sequence"},{"text":"She goes from playing quietly to playing as loudly as she can, showing she wants attention.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"},{"text":"She goes from playing without listening to fitting her sound with others, showing she now values her role in the whole.","is_correct":true},{"text":"She goes from playing alone to playing only with Hana, showing friendship matters most.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She goes from playing without listening to fitting her sound with others, showing she now values her role in the whole.$q$, $q$At first she "played it without really listening," but later she listens to the cellos and flutes and fits her sound into theirs. She learns when to "swell" and "fade," not to play as loudly as possible, so the choice about playing "as loudly as she can" misreads the details.$q$, 'draft', 'bd979aea-5281-595d-9d5a-52b19c1e442b')
