-- Passage rg6-word-parts-p01
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('1062a784-bfcb-5328-ba64-5da8d5c830ef', 'rg6-word-parts-p01', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g6-word-parts'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Relay Day$q$, $q$On the morning of the district relay meet, Keoni Kahale arrived early to help his coach. The coach asked him to inspect each baton before the races began. Keoni turned every baton slowly in his hands, looking for cracks or loose tape.

By nine o'clock, the bleachers were full of spectators. Parents waved signs, and younger brothers and sisters cheered whenever a runner passed. A volunteer carried a portable scoreboard to the finish line and set it on a folding table.

Keoni's team ran the last race of the day. His job was to run the third leg and hand the baton to Dalia, the fastest runner on the team. As Keoni neared the passing zone, he heard the crowd's noise erupt behind him. A runner from another school was catching up.

Keoni stretched out his arm, and Dalia grabbed the baton cleanly. She sprinted toward the finish line and crossed it one step ahead of the other runner. The judges studied a video of the finish and did not reject the result.

That evening, Keoni told his grandmother about the race. He said the best moment was not the finish. It was the clean pass, the one thing the team had practiced every single afternoon.$q$, 'draft')
