-- Passage rg6-word-parts-p05
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('598c7be7-aa40-5381-a913-87a5d9bd836c', 'rg6-word-parts-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g6-word-parts'), null,
        '6-8', $q$The Reporter's Notebook$q$, $q$Mateo Silva had joined the school newspaper in September, and today was his first real interview. His editor, an eighth grader named Hana, had given him an assignment. He was to talk with Ms. Adeyemi, the cafeteria manager, about the new salad bar.

Mateo arrived with a notebook and three questions. Ms. Adeyemi was friendly, but she was also busy. Twice, a worker had to interrupt the interview to ask her about a delivery. Each time, Mateo waited patiently and then picked up where they had left off.

Ms. Adeyemi talked quickly, and Mateo's handwriting could not keep up. He asked if he could record her voice and write a transcript later. She agreed, and he set the recorder on the table.

At the end, Mateo asked Ms. Adeyemi to predict how students would feel about the salad bar. She smiled and said she expected the cucumbers to disappear first.

That night, Mateo typed out every word from the recording. He found one spot where he had misheard her. She had said "fresh peppers," not "fried peppers." He was glad he could check.

Hana read his article the next day. She suggested a few small changes but said the story was ready to print. Mateo felt proud, because his name would appear right above his first story.$q$, 'draft')
