   $q$Which statement best evaluates the supporters' evidence about the town of Merrow?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It proves that a bridge would double the number of shops in Calder Falls too.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralizes"},{"text":"It is the strongest evidence, because it comes from the ferry owner himself.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It is irrelevant, because Merrow is forty miles away from Calder Falls.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misjudges-relevance"},{"text":"It suggests a bridge might help business, but other causes could explain Merrow's growth.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It suggests a bridge might help business, but other causes could explain Merrow's growth.$q$, $q$Merrow's shops doubled after its bridge was built, but the passage gives no proof that the bridge caused the growth. Claiming it proves the same result for Calder Falls stretches one example too far.$q$, 'draft', '97bbbdaf-e60f-5c37-a446-17680f7cbadf')
