   $q$Which detail supports the reason that fallen leaves are a home for small animals?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Pinecrest collects about 900 tons of yard waste every single fall.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mismatched-reason"},{"text":"Many moths and butterflies spend the winter as eggs or cocoons in leaf piles.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Leaves release nutrients that trees and other plants use in the spring.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mismatched-reason"},{"text":"A thick, wet layer of leaves can smother the grass on a lawn.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-counterclaim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Many moths and butterflies spend the winter as eggs or cocoons in leaf piles.$q$, $q$The detail about moths and butterflies is in the paragraph about leaves as a home for animals. The nutrient detail supports the separate reason that leaves feed the soil.$q$, 'draft', '01ba47a1-7811-5fb6-8e7f-90c7299862e4')
