  ('33fc36d3-b9bd-569a-9b26-fc5b78f7940f', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g7-authors-purpose'), null, 'medium',
   $q$According to the author, why do some people believe that bats are blind?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They know that bats have no eyes at all and must depend on their ears.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"They have seen fruit bats bump into trees and hills while flying at night.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They assume a bat that finds food by sound must have eyes that do not work.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They have read that bats cannot see ultraviolet light the way people can.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They assume a bat that finds food by sound must have eyes that do not work.$q$, $q$The author says people see that echolocation is impressive and "assume bats must use it because their eyes do not work." The passage says every bat has eyes, so "bats have no eyes at all" contradicts it, and it says some bats see ultraviolet light, so the claim that they cannot is wrong. Nothing mentions bats bumping into trees.$q$, 'draft', '5b5d075c-0f95-5b9b-8c2d-a0a53139d12c')
