   $q$Why does the author end the passage with "It is a creature with an extra one"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To introduce a new topic about bat senses that the author will discuss next.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"To flip the saying's idea, showing bats have more abilities rather than fewer.","is_correct":true},{"text":"To admit that the saying is partly true because bats need extra help to see.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-concession"},{"text":"To suggest that bats have a secret sense that scientists cannot yet explain.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To flip the saying's idea, showing bats have more abilities rather than fewer.$q$, $q$The saying treats bats as missing sight, and the ending turns that around: bats have sight plus echolocation. The "extra" sense is echolocation, already explained, not a mystery sense or a new topic.$q$, 'draft', '5b5d075c-0f95-5b9b-8c2d-a0a53139d12c')
