   $q$How does the final paragraph distinguish the author's priorities from those of people who support the current system?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It explains that both sides agree completely and only disagree about the number of minutes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-agreement"},{"text":"It proves that winning games has no value at all for players at the middle school level.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"exaggerates-position"},{"text":"It shows that the author cares only about winning, just as the supporters of the system do.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-position"},{"text":"It contrasts a short-term win with a lifelong love of sport, showing the author values growth more.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It contrasts a short-term win with a lifelong love of sport, showing the author values growth more.$q$, $q$The paragraph sets "feels great for an evening" against "can last a lifetime," ranking long-term growth above a single win. The author says winning "feels great," so the author does not claim winning has no value.$q$, 'draft', 'bc9354b3-3a1b-5c23-a5c7-7e0897a592a9')
