   $q$Which sentence from the passage most directly states the author's position?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"The city council will vote on the repainting plan in May.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"detail-not-claim"},{"text":"\"I propose a different plan: invite students from the three nearby schools to design and paint a mural there.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"The city's public works director has raised two concerns.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-opposing-view"},{"text":"\"The concrete walls of the Lindell Street underpass are gray, cracked, and often covered in scribbled tags.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"detail-not-claim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"I propose a different plan: invite students from the three nearby schools to design and paint a mural there."$q$, $q$The sentence beginning "I propose a different plan" says exactly what the author wants to happen. The sentence about gray, cracked walls describes the setting, the sentence about the director names her concerns, and the sentence about the May vote gives timing, so none of them states the author's position.$q$, 'draft', '149f235a-7156-50bf-a282-bd3f18a3be01')
